  "notes": [
    "Supply / Demand / EMT / % price-reduced are point-in-time from the July 28 2026 deck (Laguna Beach office meeting deck, 'ORANGE COUNTY | LAGUNA BEACH, JULY 2026'). These are the only figures that actually changed versus the July 1 deck.",
    "IMPORTANT — sold data is UNCHANGED from the July 1 deck. The July 28 deck's sold slides are titled 'JUNE 2026 SOLD' but every cell is byte-identical to the July 1 deck's 'MAY 2026 SOLD' slides (verified by diffing the extracted text of both PDFs: all 13 cities match on count, median, S/L ratio and median DOM across all three price buckets). One of the two labels is wrong at source. Deck-date logic favors the newer label (a July 28 deck should report June closings), so these are stored as sold_june_2026_*. Treat the closing figures as already-published data, not fresh news.",
    "Zillow HVI is likewise unchanged and still labeled 'May 2026 Home Prices'. Stored as zillow_hvi_may_2026 with zillow_reporting_month 2026-05.",
    "Snapshot metrics load into SQLite under reporting_month 2026-07 and therefore supersede the July 1 deck's snapshot rows for the same month/source. This is intended: the July 28 snapshot is the current one.",
    "Per-city comparison slides are titled 'Year-Over-Year Comparison'. The overview 'Y-O-Y CHANGES' column and per-city deltas are YEAR-OVER-YEAR and are stored in the legacy inventory_mom_pct / pending_mom_pct / emt_mom_days fields to preserve the pipeline; for THIS deck those legacy-named fields hold Y-o-Y values.",
    "GOTCHA — Newport Coast demand delta: the main overview slide reads '+29%' but both the North Coastal Area slide and the per-city Newport Coast slide read '-29% or -2 Pendings'. Demand fell 7 to 5, which is -29%. Using -29%.",
    "GOTCHA — Laguna Beach EMT: the per-city Laguna Beach slide reads '155 DAYS' (Irvine's EMT bleeding in). The overview and South Coastal Area slides both read 177 days, the internal math confirms it (165 homes / (28 pendings / 30) = 177), and the per-city 'Last Year: 344 Days' minus the overview delta of -167 also lands on 177. Using 177.",
    "GOTCHA — Dana Point ALL sold count: the per-city Dana Point slide reads 314 homes / $2.2m (count bleed, same corruption as the July 1 deck). The aggregate slide shows 31 homes / $2.1m and $0-5M (29) + $5M+ (2) = 31. Using 31 / $2.1m / 95.6% / 8 days.",
    "GOTCHA — Newport Beach ALL sold count: the per-city slide reads 78 homes (Laguna Niguel's count bleeding in). The aggregate slide shows 63 and $0-5M (44) + $5M+ (19) = 63. Using 63 / $3.7m / 98.2% / 26 days. ($5M+ median $7.2m from the aggregate slide vs $7.1m per-city; used $7.2m, consistent with the July 1 ingest.)",
    "GOTCHA — Irvine Zillow HVI: the North Coastal Area HVI slide again shows -1.4% / -12.3% / +55.7%. The main HOME PRICE SNAPSHOT slide shows -0.1% / -1.2% / +55.7%. Using the main-snapshot values.",
    "Coto De Caza is newly present in this ingest. It appears on the July 28 overview, price-reduction, HVI and all three sold slides; it was skipped in the July 1 file. Values are internally consistent across slides (55 homes / 12 pendings / 138 days EMT; 138 = 55 / (12/30)).",
    "Minor rounding: Huntington Beach (overview +11 vs slide 80-70=10), Laguna Niguel (-5 vs 85-91=-6) and San Juan Capistrano (+6 vs 103-98=+5) each differ by a day. Source rounding; overview delta stored in emt_mom_days, per-city 'Last Year' stored in expected_market_time_days_last_year.",
    "San Clemente is internally consistent: inventory 122 (-24%, -38 homes, last year 160); demand 52 (+6%, +3 pendings, last year 49); EMT 70 (122 / (52/30) = 70), last year 98, delta -28. Price reductions 40%.",
    "San Clemente movement since the July 1 deck: inventory flat at 122, demand 54 to 52, EMT 68 to 70, and share of listings with a price cut 34% to 40%. The price-cut jump is the notable four-week change.",
    "This deck has NO national/macro section. The back half is a DRE advertising-compliance training module (disclosure requirements, team/FBN rules, fair housing, AB 723 digitally-altered-image disclosure). All national.* fields remain null.",
    "OC-wide reduction_breakdown is carried forward from the July 1 deck (Reports on Housing, Orange County - June 2026); the July 28 deck does not reprint it."
  ],
